chapter.v:
	Do not 

	 be envious of evil men,Nor desire to be with them;
 [Ezek. 2:8,]

	Through wisdom 

	 a house is built,And by understanding it is established;
 [Jer. 15:16; Rev. 10:9 c Ps. 19:10;]

	My son, 

	 eat honey because it is good,And the honeycomb which is sweet to your taste;
 [Ezek. 1:24;]

	Do not 

	 lie in wait, O wicked man, against the dwelling of the righteous;Do not plunder his resting place;
 [Job 2:13; Ps.]

	Do not 

	 rejoice when your enemy falls,And do not let your heart be glad when he stumbles;
 [Ezek. 33:7-9] [Is. 52:8; 56:10; Jer. 6:17 r [Lev. 19:17; Prov. 14:25]; Is. 58:1]

	Do not 

	 fret because of evildoers,Nor be envious of the wicked;
 [Is. 49:4, 5; Ezek. 14:14, 20; Acts 18:6; 20:26; 1 Tim. 4:16]
